WEBVTT

00:11:51.869 --> 00:11:52.967
Look, dad's gone now.

00:11:52.969 --> 00:11:54.668
We have to carry out his legacy,

00:11:54.668 --> 00:11:58.168
And that means hunting down as many
evil sons of bitches as we possibly can.

00:12:00.469 --> 00:12:01.268
Did I die?

00:12:01.269 --> 00:12:02.967
Did you sell your soul for me?

00:12:02.969 --> 00:12:03.969
How long do you get?

00:12:04.168 --> 00:12:04.969
One year.

00:12:05.168 --> 00:12:06.269
You shouldn't have done that.

00:12:07.369 --> 00:12:09.469
I guess I got to save your ass
for a change.

00:12:11.769 --> 00:12:13.769
What kind of blade
can kill a demon?

00:12:14.068 --> 00:12:15.967
Yesterday, I would have
said there was no such thing.

00:12:15.969 --> 00:12:17.369
Who was that masked chick?

00:12:17.469 --> 00:12:19.368
You ever run across a guy
named Gordon Walker?

00:12:19.369 --> 00:12:21.967
He is dangerous to everyone
and everything around him.

00:12:21.969 --> 00:12:23.967
This demon tells me
they have soldiers

00:12:23.969 --> 00:12:25.768
to fight in this coming war

00:12:25.769 --> 00:12:27.668
humans fighting on hell's side.

00:12:27.668 --> 00:12:29.668
I know about Sam's visions.

00:12:29.668 --> 00:12:31.967
I know everything,
and your brother's fair game.

00:12:31.969 --> 00:12:32.869
Aaah!

00:12:43.068 --> 00:12:45.668
Gordon should be reaching for the soap
for the next few years, at least.

00:12:45.668 --> 00:12:47.269
Tell me who you are!

00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:50.668
You're a demon.

00:12:50.668 --> 00:12:51.467
I'm here

00:12:51.469 --> 00:12:52.668
because I want to help you.

00:12:52.668 --> 00:12:54.067
What could you possibly...

00:12:54.068 --> 00:12:56.068
I can help you
save your brother.

00:13:07.969 --> 00:13:14.094
<font color="#4096d1">Supernatural 3x03 Bad day at Black Rock
==ragbear.com==</font>

00:13:26.469 --> 00:13:27.469
It's true.

00:13:27.769 --> 00:13:30.068
The devil's gate
was opened in Wyoming.

00:13:32.969 --> 00:13:34.168
Big...

00:13:36.568 --> 00:13:38.269
St. Helens big.

00:13:39.969 --> 00:13:42.568
There's no solid fix
on how many demons got out,

00:13:42.668 --> 00:13:44.568
but it's in the hundreds...
an army.

00:13:44.668 --> 00:13:46.568
Sam Winchester was there,

00:13:46.668 --> 00:13:47.568
wasn't he?

00:13:49.469 --> 00:13:52.268
Talked to a guy who knows guy
who knows Bobby Singer,

00:13:52.269 --> 00:13:54.868
and, yeah, looks like the
Winchesters were at ground zero

00:13:54.869 --> 00:13:56.269
when the gate was popped.

00:13:56.869 --> 00:13:59.168
But singer said
they went in there to stop it.

00:13:59.168 --> 00:14:00.369
mnh-mnh.

00:14:00.469 --> 00:14:02.269
Bobby's edge ain't what it used to be.

00:14:02.469 --> 00:14:04.468
Sam could have him believing
anything by now.

00:14:04.469 --> 00:14:05.468
Listen, Gordon.

00:14:05.469 --> 00:14:06.968
As far as talk goes,

00:14:06.969 --> 00:14:08.568
Sam Winchester checks out.

00:14:09.469 --> 00:14:10.768
He's a hunter. That's all.

00:14:10.769 --> 00:14:11.568
That's all?

00:14:15.469 --> 00:14:16.369
Kubrick...

00:14:17.168 --> 00:14:18.869
I'm not even sure he's human.

00:14:20.568 --> 00:14:21.568
Think I'm crazy?

00:14:22.369 --> 00:14:24.168
I told you there was a war coming

00:14:24.168 --> 00:14:25.269
six months ago.

00:14:25.668 --> 00:14:26.969
Take a look around.

00:14:27.568 --> 00:14:28.668
It's here.

00:14:29.568 --> 00:14:32.469
Now I'm telling you this boy
is a part of it.

00:14:33.369 --> 00:14:35.068
Track him down, Kubrick.

00:14:35.668 --> 00:14:37.068
You'll come to see it, too.

00:14:38.869 --> 00:14:40.969
Sam Winchester must die.

00:14:53.769 --> 00:14:55.168
Because demon, that's why.

00:14:55.168 --> 00:14:57.468
I mean, the second you find out
this ruby chick is a demon,

00:14:57.469 --> 00:14:58.768
You go for the holy water.

00:14:58.769 --> 00:15:00.968
- You don't chat.
- No one was chatting, Dean.

00:15:00.969 --> 00:15:02.867
Oh, yeah? Then why didn't
you send her ass back to hell?

00:15:02.869 --> 00:15:05.668
Because... Because she said she
might be able to help us out.

00:15:05.668 --> 00:15:06.469
How?

00:15:08.369 --> 00:15:10.567
Oh, really, Sam? How?
How could she possibly help us?

00:15:10.568 --> 00:15:12.369
She told me she could help you, okay?

00:15:14.068 --> 00:15:15.869
Help you out of the crossroads deal.

00:15:18.869 --> 00:15:20.468
What's wrong with you? She's lying.

00:15:20.469 --> 00:15:22.068
You got to know that, don't you?

00:15:23.168 --> 00:15:25.269
She knows what your weakness is.
It's me.

00:15:27.568 --> 00:15:28.668
What else did she say?

00:15:30.769 --> 00:15:32.469
- Dude?
- Nothing.

00:15:33.969 --> 00:15:35.469
Nothing, okay?!

00:15:35.969 --> 00:15:36.968
Look, I'm not an idiot, Dean.

00:15:36.969 --> 00:15:38.568
I'm not talking about trusting her.

00:15:38.769 --> 00:15:40.469
I'm talking about using her.

00:15:40.769 --> 00:15:42.068
I mean, we're at war, right?

00:15:42.369 --> 00:15:43.768
And we don't know Jack about the enemy.

00:15:43.769 --> 00:15:44.768
We don't know where they are.

00:15:44.769 --> 00:15:46.067
We don't know what they're doing.

00:15:46.068 --> 00:15:47.668
Hell, we don't even know what they want.

00:15:47.869 --> 00:15:48.968
Now, this Ruby girl

00:15:48.969 --> 00:15:51.469
knows more than we will
ever find out on our own.

00:15:51.869 --> 00:15:53.168
Now, yes, it's a risk. I know that.

00:15:53.168 --> 00:15:54.469
But we need to take it.

00:15:56.668 --> 00:15:58.067
You're okay, right?
I mean, you're feeling okay?

00:15:58.068 --> 00:16:00.869
Yes, I'm fine! Why are you
always asking me that?

00:16:03.469 --> 00:16:04.568
It's not mine.

00:16:06.668 --> 00:16:07.568
Nope.

00:16:08.568 --> 00:16:10.268
Check the glove compartment.
It's dad's.

00:16:10.269 --> 00:16:11.268
- Dad's?
- Yes.

00:16:11.269 --> 00:16:13.668
I keep it charged in case
any of his old contacts call.

00:16:19.869 --> 00:16:20.769
Hello?

00:16:21.369 --> 00:16:23.469
Yes, this is Edgar Casey.

00:16:25.269 --> 00:16:28.168
No, no, no, no. Don't... don't call the 
police. I'll handle this myself.

00:16:29.269 --> 00:16:29.867
Thanks.

00:16:29.869 --> 00:16:32.869
You know, can you just...
can you just lock it back up for me?

00:16:33.668 --> 00:16:34.469
Great.

00:16:34.668 --> 00:16:37.567
Uh, I... I don't have my...
my book in front of me.

00:16:37.568 --> 00:16:39.869
Do you... do you have
the address so I can...

00:16:40.168 --> 00:16:41.469
Sure. Okay.

00:16:41.568 --> 00:16:42.668
Go ahead.

00:16:44.869 --> 00:16:45.768
Right.

00:16:45.769 --> 00:16:46.668
Thanks a lot.

00:16:49.168 --> 00:16:51.468
Dad ever tell you he kept a container
at a storage place?

00:16:51.469 --> 00:16:53.269
- What?
- Outside of Buffalo.

00:16:53.969 --> 00:16:54.668
No way.

00:16:54.668 --> 00:16:55.468
Yeah.

00:16:55.469 --> 00:16:57.068
And someone just broke into it.

00:17:11.969 --> 00:17:14.568
So, you've got no hard evidence
on this Winchester guy?

00:17:14.668 --> 00:17:16.969
You're just working off
Gordon's instincts.

00:17:17.068 --> 00:17:18.469
You ever hunt with Gordon?

00:17:18.568 --> 00:17:20.469
No. I heard he's good.

00:17:20.568 --> 00:17:21.969
Good?

00:17:22.668 --> 00:17:23.367
He's the best.

00:17:23.369 --> 00:17:25.469
Saved my ass more times
than I can count.

00:17:25.869 --> 00:17:28.369
So, if he says
Sam Winchester's dangerous,

00:17:28.869 --> 00:17:29.867
I believe him.

00:17:29.869 --> 00:17:31.568
He's gonna be covering his tracks.

00:17:31.668 --> 00:17:32.869
Won't be easy to find.

00:17:33.068 --> 00:17:36.168
Last I got puts him in Nebraska
three weeks back.

00:17:36.168 --> 00:17:37.469
Not exactly a fresh lead.

00:17:37.568 --> 00:17:39.367
He ain't invisible, creedie.

00:17:39.369 --> 00:17:41.168
Some hunter out there knows something.

00:17:41.769 --> 00:17:43.869
So we start calling our contacts.

00:17:44.668 --> 00:17:46.469
All we need is one break.

00:18:01.269 --> 00:18:02.869
Don't play with my Jesus.

00:18:08.168 --> 00:18:09.168
Man.

00:18:10.568 --> 00:18:11.369
What?

00:18:12.168 --> 00:18:14.369
Just dad. You know, him and his secrets.

00:18:14.869 --> 00:18:16.168
We spent all this time with this guy,

00:18:16.168 --> 00:18:17.567
and it's like we barely even 
know the man.

00:18:17.568 --> 00:18:19.769
Well, we're about to learn something.

00:18:35.769 --> 00:18:37.168
No demons allowed.

00:18:39.568 --> 00:18:40.568
Blood.

00:18:44.369 --> 00:18:45.568
Check this out.

00:18:54.068 --> 00:18:56.168
Whoever broke in here got attacked.

00:18:58.369 --> 00:18:59.568
Dear, old dad.

00:19:01.269 --> 00:19:02.567
I got two sets of boot tracks.

00:19:02.568 --> 00:19:04.668
It looks like it was a two-man job.

00:19:05.369 --> 00:19:06.867
And our friend with the buckshot 
in him...

00:19:06.869 --> 00:19:08.568
It looks like he kept walking.

00:19:10.168 --> 00:19:11.168
So, what's the deal?

00:19:11.168 --> 00:19:12.869
Dad would do work here or something?

00:19:13.769 --> 00:19:15.668
Living the high life, as usual.

00:19:33.869 --> 00:19:35.367
1995.

00:19:35.369 --> 00:19:36.568
No way!

00:19:38.269 --> 00:19:40.969
That's my division championship
soccer trophy.

00:19:42.568 --> 00:19:44.068
I can't believe he kept this.

00:19:44.369 --> 00:19:47.269
It was the probably the closest
you ever came to being a boy.

00:19:49.469 --> 00:19:50.969
Oh, wow!

00:19:54.269 --> 00:19:56.668
It's my first sawed-off.
I made it myself.

00:19:57.469 --> 00:19:58.769
Sixth grade.

00:20:15.769 --> 00:20:17.469
Holy crap.

00:20:20.168 --> 00:20:21.869
Look at this.
He had land mines...

00:20:23.168 --> 00:20:24.568
Which they didn't take.

00:20:26.469 --> 00:20:27.769
Or the guns.

00:20:29.469 --> 00:20:31.168
Guess they knew what they were after ?

00:20:35.168 --> 00:20:36.369
Hey, Dean, check this out.

00:20:37.469 --> 00:20:38.469
See these symbols?

00:20:39.469 --> 00:20:40.869
He used binding magic.

00:20:42.869 --> 00:20:44.469
These are curse boxes.

00:20:44.668 --> 00:20:45.768
Curse boxes?

00:20:45.769 --> 00:20:47.467
They're supposed to keep
the evil mojo in, right?

00:20:47.469 --> 00:20:48.467
Kind of like the pandora deal.

00:20:48.469 --> 00:20:51.469
Yeah, they're built to contain
the power of the cursed object.

00:20:51.568 --> 00:20:53.367
Dad's journal did mention
a whole bunch of stuff,

00:20:53.369 --> 00:20:55.867
You know, dangerous,
hexed items, fetishes.

00:20:55.869 --> 00:20:57.268
He never did say
where they ended up.

00:20:57.269 --> 00:20:57.967
Yeah.

00:20:57.969 --> 00:21:00.168
This must be his toxic-waste dump.

00:21:08.469 --> 00:21:09.769
One box is missing.

00:21:10.869 --> 00:21:11.668
Great.

00:21:12.668 --> 00:21:14.067
Well, maybe they didn't open it.

00:21:14.068 --> 00:21:15.268
Come on, man.
Let's open it.

00:21:15.269 --> 00:21:17.768
Shut up about the damn box!

00:21:17.769 --> 00:21:19.268
Do you see what's happening here?

00:21:19.269 --> 00:21:21.969
I'm literally bleeding to death.

00:21:22.168 --> 00:21:23.969
- I'm gonna open it.
- Grossman...

00:21:24.269 --> 00:21:26.068
Look, what if this
is really worth something?

00:21:26.269 --> 00:21:28.568
What, we should
just hand it over to her?

00:21:28.969 --> 00:21:30.469
We took all the risk.

00:21:30.568 --> 00:21:31.568
Hell, Wayne,

00:21:31.668 --> 00:21:32.969
you got shot,

00:21:33.269 --> 00:21:35.369
and all for a lousy few hundred bucks.

00:21:35.668 --> 00:21:39.369
Now, we could make more selling
whatever it is ourselves.

00:21:59.568 --> 00:22:00.469
Huh?

00:22:01.269 --> 00:22:02.168
Are you kidding me?

00:22:02.168 --> 00:22:03.469
Are you kidding me?!

00:22:06.869 --> 00:22:07.967
It's a rabbit's foot.

00:22:07.969 --> 00:22:10.068
It's a rabbit's foot, Grossman!

00:22:11.969 --> 00:22:13.969
I'm gonna die for a damn rabbit's foot.

00:22:23.469 --> 00:22:24.469
Oh.

00:22:26.168 --> 00:22:27.168
Hey, Foster.

00:22:27.269 --> 00:22:29.367
Hey, listen, guys,
not to be a drag or nothing,

00:22:29.369 --> 00:22:30.567
but it's 6:00 in the morning.

00:22:30.568 --> 00:22:31.467
- Right.
- Can't you guys keep it down?

00:22:31.469 --> 00:22:34.068
No, we just got a situation here is all.
Sorry.

00:22:34.568 --> 00:22:35.769
What the hell happened to you?

00:22:36.068 --> 00:22:37.369
A shotgun happened to me.

00:22:41.568 --> 00:22:42.768
- Hey, Grossman,
- Yeah?

00:22:42.769 --> 00:22:44.568
Under my sink, there's a medical kit.

00:22:44.969 --> 00:22:46.269
And get some water boiling.

00:22:49.668 --> 00:22:51.769
I used to be an army medic,
you know, in nam.

00:22:52.668 --> 00:22:54.469
So, I guess this is your lucky day.

00:23:18.969 --> 00:23:19.869
Connecticut.

00:23:20.068 --> 00:23:21.668
Last three digits 8-8-0.

00:23:22.269 --> 00:23:23.668
Yep. That's it.

00:23:25.269 --> 00:23:26.367
Should have blacked out their plates

00:23:26.369 --> 00:23:28.769
Before they parked in front of
the security camera.

00:23:30.469 --> 00:23:31.469
Four kings.

00:23:32.269 --> 00:23:33.269
You see that?

00:23:33.469 --> 00:23:35.068
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:23:35.668 --> 00:23:36.668
Deal it up again.

00:23:45.969 --> 00:23:46.967
Royal flush.

00:23:46.969 --> 00:23:50.269
Grossman, that's the second
royal flush in eight hands.

00:23:53.869 --> 00:23:55.068
I can't lose.

00:23:55.568 --> 00:23:58.869
I mean, really,
I... I can't lose.

00:23:59.369 --> 00:24:00.769
I think this thing really works.

00:24:01.668 --> 00:24:02.568
You know what I'm saying?

00:24:03.369 --> 00:24:05.068
I'll tell you one thing...
there's no way in hell

00:24:05.568 --> 00:24:07.369
we are handing it over
to that stuck-up bitch.

00:24:11.769 --> 00:24:12.668
- Freeze! - Freeze!

00:24:12.668 --> 00:24:13.467
Nobody move!

00:24:13.469 --> 00:24:14.867
- Don't move.
- Don't move!

00:24:14.869 --> 00:24:16.168
- What is it?
- Stop!

00:24:16.969 --> 00:24:18.567
All right. Give us the box.

00:24:18.568 --> 00:24:20.168
Please tell me that you didn't...

00:24:20.168 --> 00:24:21.168
Oh, they did.

00:24:24.269 --> 00:24:25.269
You opened it?!

00:24:26.369 --> 00:24:27.367
Are you guys cops?

00:24:27.369 --> 00:24:28.467
- Huh?
- Are you guys cops?!

00:24:28.469 --> 00:24:29.769
What was in the box?

00:24:32.969 --> 00:24:35.168
Oh, was that it, huh?
It was, wasn't it?

00:24:35.769 --> 00:24:36.769
What is that thing?

00:24:49.068 --> 00:24:49.769
Sorry.

00:25:18.668 --> 00:25:19.568
Dean...

00:25:20.369 --> 00:25:21.168
I got it.

00:25:22.369 --> 00:25:23.369
No, you don't.

00:25:32.769 --> 00:25:33.568
Damn!

00:25:35.168 --> 00:25:36.068
Whoa!

00:25:41.969 --> 00:25:42.668
Sam!

00:25:55.469 --> 00:25:56.668
That's a lucky break.

00:25:58.769 --> 00:25:59.869
Is that a rabbit's foot?

00:26:02.668 --> 00:26:03.769
I think it is.

00:26:05.369 --> 00:26:06.168
Huh.

00:26:20.769 --> 00:26:22.869
I'm not finding anything on it
in dad's journal.

00:26:26.369 --> 00:26:28.268
- Dean, come on.
- What?

00:26:28.269 --> 00:26:30.367
Hey, that was my gun
he was aiming at your head.

00:26:30.369 --> 00:26:32.768
and my gun don't jam,
so that was a lucky break.

00:26:32.769 --> 00:26:35.769
Not to mention them taking themselves 
out... also a lucky break.

00:26:37.469 --> 00:26:38.869
Here. Scratch one.

00:26:39.969 --> 00:26:40.969
Come on, Sam.

00:26:41.269 --> 00:26:42.168
Scratch and win.

00:26:44.769 --> 00:26:46.769
Look, Dean, it's got to be
cursed somehow.

00:26:47.769 --> 00:26:49.668
Otherwise, dad wouldn't 
have locked it up.

00:26:52.969 --> 00:26:54.269
$1,200.

00:26:54.869 --> 00:26:56.369
You just won $1,200.

00:26:58.769 --> 00:26:59.969
Whoo!

00:27:00.769 --> 00:27:02.568
I don't know, man.
It doesn't seem that cursed to me.

00:27:19.969 --> 00:27:21.068
Grossman?

00:27:22.469 --> 00:27:23.568
Grossman, get up.

00:27:27.469 --> 00:27:28.369
Hey...

00:27:29.168 --> 00:27:30.068
Grossman, get up.

00:27:34.168 --> 00:27:34.969
Hey.

00:28:08.369 --> 00:28:09.369
Hey...

00:28:12.269 --> 00:28:13.068
Grossman?

00:28:22.068 --> 00:28:22.969
Oh.

00:28:28.269 --> 00:28:29.769
Ahhh!

00:28:33.168 --> 00:28:34.369
Oh, man.

00:28:34.769 --> 00:28:36.067
Now, look, Bobby, we didn't know.

00:28:36.068 --> 00:28:38.067
You touched it? Damn it, Sam.

00:28:38.068 --> 00:28:39.769
Well, dad never told us
about this thing.

00:28:40.269 --> 00:28:42.367
I mean, you knew about
a storage place in Black Rock?

00:28:42.369 --> 00:28:43.867
His lockup? Yeah, I knew.

00:28:43.869 --> 00:28:45.969
Hell, I built those curse boxes for him.

00:28:46.369 --> 00:28:49.467
Listen, you have got a serious problem.

00:28:49.469 --> 00:28:52.068
That rabbit's foot ain't 
no dime-store notion.

00:28:53.168 --> 00:28:55.969
It's real hoodoo... old-world stuff.

00:28:56.169 --> 00:28:59.469
Made by a Baton Rouge conjure
woman about 100 years ago.

00:28:59.568 --> 00:29:01.068
It's a hell of a luck charm.

00:29:01.169 --> 00:29:02.968
It's not a luck charm.
It's a curse.

00:29:02.969 --> 00:29:04.868
She made it to kill people, Sam.

00:29:05.068 --> 00:29:05.868
See,

00:29:06.169 --> 00:29:08.269
you touch it, you own it.

00:29:08.469 --> 00:29:12.169
You own it, sure, you get a run
of good luck to beat the devil.

00:29:12.368 --> 00:29:13.067
But...

00:29:13.068 --> 00:29:15.568
you lose it, that luck turns.

00:29:15.868 --> 00:29:18.567
It turns so bad that 
you're dead inside a week.

00:29:18.568 --> 00:29:19.968
So, I won't lose it, Bobby.

00:29:19.969 --> 00:29:21.468
Everybody loses it!

00:29:21.469 --> 00:29:23.269
Well, then, how do we break the curse?

00:29:24.269 --> 00:29:25.769
I don't know if you can.

00:29:27.068 --> 00:29:29.969
Let me look through my library
and make some calls.

00:29:30.669 --> 00:29:31.969
Just sit tight.

00:29:34.868 --> 00:29:35.868
Dude,

00:29:36.568 --> 00:29:38.169
we're up 15 grand.

00:29:45.669 --> 00:29:46.268
Don't worry.

00:29:46.269 --> 00:29:47.867
Bobby will find a way to break it.

00:29:47.868 --> 00:29:50.669
Till then, I say we hit Vegas,
pull a little "Rain Man."

00:29:50.868 --> 00:29:51.667
You can be Rain Man.

00:29:51.669 --> 00:29:54.068
We just lay low until 
Bobby calls back, okay?

00:29:54.169 --> 00:29:55.867
Hi. Uh, table for two, please.

00:29:55.868 --> 00:29:58.269
Congratulations!

00:29:58.368 --> 00:29:59.468
Say that again?

00:29:59.469 --> 00:30:03.868
You are the one millionth guest
of the Biggerson's restaurant family.

00:30:12.169 --> 00:30:13.969
Right. If you hear anything,
give me a call.

00:30:14.868 --> 00:30:16.469
Well, that clears my book.

00:30:16.669 --> 00:30:17.969
The word's out.

00:30:18.068 --> 00:30:19.568
Now we wait.

00:30:19.868 --> 00:30:21.068
Now we eat.

00:30:21.469 --> 00:30:22.469
Good idea.

00:30:23.169 --> 00:30:24.667
What do you like?
I got canned everything.

00:30:24.669 --> 00:30:27.368
No, no, man.
Not eating in the r.v.

00:30:27.469 --> 00:30:28.969
Look, I know a good place.

00:30:29.469 --> 00:30:32.368
Wide menu, good service,
homey atmosphere...

00:30:32.769 --> 00:30:33.769
Garlic knots.

00:30:34.469 --> 00:30:36.469
The menu's on their website.

00:30:38.368 --> 00:30:39.469
Bobby's right.

00:30:39.669 --> 00:30:41.469
This lore goes way back.

00:30:41.868 --> 00:30:42.868
Pure hoodoo.

00:30:43.868 --> 00:30:45.868
You can't just cut one off any rabbit.

00:30:46.068 --> 00:30:47.568
It has to be in a cemetery

00:30:47.669 --> 00:30:50.368
under a full moon on a friday the 13th.

00:30:52.568 --> 00:30:53.669
I think from now on,

00:30:54.068 --> 00:30:56.068
we only go to places with Biggerson's.

00:31:04.469 --> 00:31:05.568
Can I freshen you up?

00:31:06.068 --> 00:31:07.169
Yeah. Yeah, sure.

00:31:10.868 --> 00:31:11.568
Thanks.

00:31:13.269 --> 00:31:14.669
- Oh.
- Oh.

00:31:14.868 --> 00:31:17.969
Oh, I... No, don't worry.
That's okay. That's... I got it.

00:31:18.568 --> 00:31:20.368
It's no trouble, really.

00:31:20.769 --> 00:31:21.568
Okay.

00:31:21.868 --> 00:31:22.868
Sorry about that.

00:31:23.169 --> 00:31:24.169
It's all right.

00:31:43.769 --> 00:31:44.568
Dude,

00:31:44.868 --> 00:31:46.669
if you were ever gonna get lucky...

00:31:47.568 --> 00:31:48.469
Chill out.

00:31:51.969 --> 00:31:53.868
Oh! Oh, jeez!

00:31:57.269 --> 00:31:58.269
Sorry.

00:32:00.969 --> 00:32:02.269
How was that good?

00:32:07.469 --> 00:32:08.769
Son of a bitch.

00:32:22.669 --> 00:32:23.469
Come on.

00:32:25.868 --> 00:32:26.669
Whoa!

00:32:31.169 --> 00:32:31.969
Wow.

00:32:32.068 --> 00:32:33.068
You suck.

00:32:35.969 --> 00:32:37.669
So, what, now your luck turns bad?

00:32:40.269 --> 00:32:41.068
I guess.

00:32:44.269 --> 00:32:45.368
I wonder how bad.

00:32:49.469 --> 00:32:50.067
Looks good.

00:32:50.068 --> 00:32:52.368
I like that when they drop
the whole onion in the fryer.

00:32:53.269 --> 00:32:55.169
Nearest location...

00:33:02.368 --> 00:33:03.469
You seeing that?

00:33:08.969 --> 00:33:10.169
Yes, I am.

00:33:19.568 --> 00:33:21.068
<i>Adios compadre.</i>

00:33:33.568 --> 00:33:35.068
Oh, man.

00:33:35.669 --> 00:33:36.969
What do you want?

00:33:37.068 --> 00:33:38.269
Heard about your friend.

00:33:38.669 --> 00:33:39.669
It's bad luck.

00:33:41.269 --> 00:33:42.469
Piss off.

00:33:42.868 --> 00:33:45.769
We know someone hired you
to steal the rabbit's foot...

00:33:45.868 --> 00:33:46.568
A woman.

00:33:46.868 --> 00:33:47.669
Yeah?

00:33:48.669 --> 00:33:49.669
How do you know that?

00:33:49.868 --> 00:33:51.868
Because she just stole it back from us.

00:33:54.068 --> 00:33:55.269
Listen, man, this is...

00:34:00.068 --> 00:34:01.068
Sam, you okay?

00:34:01.169 --> 00:34:02.068
Yeah. I'm good.

00:34:06.669 --> 00:34:08.469
I want you to tell us her name.

00:34:09.568 --> 00:34:10.668
Screw you.

00:34:13.368 --> 00:34:15.568
It wasn't a freak accident
that killed your partner.

00:34:16.168 --> 00:34:17.068
What?

00:34:17.269 --> 00:34:18.568
It was the rabbit's foot.

00:34:20.868 --> 00:34:22.068
You're crazy, man.

00:34:23.168 --> 00:34:24.168
You know I'm not.

00:34:24.769 --> 00:34:26.367
You saw what happened, what it did...

00:34:26.368 --> 00:34:28.168
All the flukes, all the luck.

00:34:28.568 --> 00:34:30.868
When you lose the foot,
that luck goes sour.

00:34:31.168 --> 00:34:32.769
That's what killed your friend.

00:34:34.668 --> 00:34:36.368
And my brother here is next,

00:34:36.969 --> 00:34:39.068
and who knows how many more
innocent people after that.

00:34:40.168 --> 00:34:41.268
Now, if you don't help us
stop this thing,

00:34:41.269 --> 00:34:43.168
then that puts those deaths 
on your head.

00:34:45.469 --> 00:34:46.668
Now, I can read people...

00:34:48.769 --> 00:34:49.568
and I get it.

00:34:50.269 --> 00:34:51.867
You're a thief and a scumbag.

00:34:51.868 --> 00:34:52.769
That's fine.

00:34:54.269 --> 00:34:55.568
But you're not a killer...

00:34:56.469 --> 00:34:57.269
Are you?

00:35:07.868 --> 00:35:09.969
No one saw which way they went,

00:35:10.368 --> 00:35:13.368
and their meal was free,
so there's no credit-card trail.

00:35:14.068 --> 00:35:15.768
Don't worry. We'll find them.

00:35:15.769 --> 00:35:17.269
What makes you so sure?

00:35:17.568 --> 00:35:20.269
'cause there's a higher power 
at work here.

00:35:20.769 --> 00:35:22.068
I know it now.

00:35:30.868 --> 00:35:31.875
Hello.

00:35:31.969 --> 00:35:33.269
Dean, great news.

00:35:33.568 --> 00:35:37.667
Wasn't easy, but I found a heavyweight
cleansing ritual that should do the trick.

00:35:37.668 --> 00:35:40.668
Bobby, that's, uh, great,
except Sam, uh...

00:35:43.068 --> 00:35:43.967
...Sam lost the foot.

00:35:43.969 --> 00:35:45.068
He what?

00:35:45.168 --> 00:35:45.967
Bobby, listen, listen.

00:35:45.969 --> 00:35:48.167
This hot chick stole it from him.

00:35:48.168 --> 00:35:49.368
I'm serious.

00:35:49.769 --> 00:35:51.667
In her mid-20s, and she was sharp, 
you know?

00:35:51.668 --> 00:35:53.368
Good enough of a con to play us.

00:35:53.668 --> 00:35:55.667
And she only gave the guys 
she hired a name...

00:35:55.668 --> 00:35:57.167
Probably an alias or something.

00:35:57.168 --> 00:35:58.668
Luigi or something.

00:35:59.269 --> 00:36:00.068
Lugosi.

00:36:00.068 --> 00:36:01.068
Lugosi?

00:36:01.269 --> 00:36:02.269
Lugosi.

00:36:04.668 --> 00:36:07.269
Oh, crap. It's probably Bela.

00:36:09.068 --> 00:36:10.768
Bela Lugosi? That's cute.

00:36:10.769 --> 00:36:12.568
Bela Talbot's her real name.

00:36:12.769 --> 00:36:14.668
Crossed paths with her once or twice.

00:36:15.068 --> 00:36:16.467
She knew about the rabbit's foot.
Is she a hunter?

00:36:16.469 --> 00:36:18.268
Pretty friggin' far from a hunter,

00:36:18.269 --> 00:36:20.168
but she knows her way
around the territory.

00:36:20.568 --> 00:36:21.467
She's been out of the country.

00:36:21.469 --> 00:36:23.769
Last I heard, she was
in the middle east someplace.

00:36:23.969 --> 00:36:25.269
I guess she's back.

00:36:25.668 --> 00:36:28.068
Which means seriously bad luck for you.

00:36:28.368 --> 00:36:29.168
Great.

00:36:29.568 --> 00:36:31.269
But if it is Bela,

00:36:31.668 --> 00:36:34.368
at least I might know some folks
who know where to find her.

00:36:34.568 --> 00:36:35.969
Thanks, Bobby, again.

00:36:36.568 --> 00:36:39.469
Just look out for your brother,
you idjit.

00:36:44.769 --> 00:36:45.568
What?

00:36:46.168 --> 00:36:47.368
I lost my shoe.

00:37:00.068 --> 00:37:03.068
All right, Bobby, thanks.
Hey, we owe you...another one.

00:37:04.168 --> 00:37:05.667
All right, Bobby's got it
on pretty good authority

00:37:05.668 --> 00:37:09.269
that this Bela chick lives in Queens.

00:37:09.668 --> 00:37:11.668
So it will take me about two hours
to get there.

00:37:12.969 --> 00:37:14.068
So, what are we doing then?

00:37:14.568 --> 00:37:15.967
You, my brother, are staying here,

00:37:15.969 --> 00:37:17.969
'cause I don't want
your bad luck getting us killed.

00:37:32.668 --> 00:37:34.068
What am I even supposed to do, Dean?

00:37:34.068 --> 00:37:35.668
Nothing. Nothing. Come here.

00:37:36.368 --> 00:37:37.867
I don't want you doing anything.

00:37:37.868 --> 00:37:40.269
I want you to sit right here

00:37:40.368 --> 00:37:42.269
and don't move, okay?

00:37:42.668 --> 00:37:44.568
Don't turn on the light.
Don't turn off the light.

00:37:44.868 --> 00:37:46.368
Don't even scratch your nose.

00:38:08.469 --> 00:38:11.168
Because you shook on 1.5.

00:38:13.568 --> 00:38:15.568
Well, maybe I should just take it 
somewhere else.

00:38:18.568 --> 00:38:20.168
Don't threaten me, Luke.

00:38:22.269 --> 00:38:24.168
Despite your reputation,
you don't scare me.

00:38:27.269 --> 00:38:28.969
Well, I'm glad you see it that way.

00:38:29.168 --> 00:38:31.068
I'll see you at the airstrip in an hour.

00:39:18.368 --> 00:39:19.868
???

00:39:43.568 --> 00:39:45.068
Oh, come on. I...

00:39:46.269 --> 00:39:47.168
I didn't...

00:40:33.368 --> 00:40:34.269
Ah!

00:40:51.068 --> 00:40:52.368
You're gonna give it back.

00:40:54.068 --> 00:40:54.868
Sweetie,

00:40:55.168 --> 00:40:56.168
no, I'm not.

00:40:57.568 --> 00:40:58.568
Yeah? We'll see.

00:40:58.668 --> 00:40:59.668
Bela, right?

00:41:00.168 --> 00:41:00.969
That's right...

00:41:01.668 --> 00:41:02.568
Dean.

00:41:05.969 --> 00:41:08.168
You know the thing's cursed,
don't you?

00:41:08.668 --> 00:41:11.367
You'd be surprised what some people
would pay for something like that.

00:41:11.368 --> 00:41:12.068
Really?

00:41:12.769 --> 00:41:14.668
There's a lucrative market out there.

00:41:15.368 --> 00:41:16.769
A lot of money to be made.

00:41:19.368 --> 00:41:22.068
You hunters, with all those amulets
and talismans you use

00:41:22.068 --> 00:41:23.668
to stop those big, bad monsters...

00:41:24.269 --> 00:41:27.867
Any one of them could put your 
children's children through college.

00:41:27.868 --> 00:41:29.269
So, you know the truth

00:41:30.269 --> 00:41:31.667
about what's really going on out there,

00:41:31.668 --> 00:41:33.668
and this is what you decide 
to do with it?

00:41:35.668 --> 00:41:37.068
You become a thief.

00:41:38.868 --> 00:41:42.068
I procure unique items
for a select clientele.

00:41:42.368 --> 00:41:43.068
Yeah.

00:41:43.168 --> 00:41:44.167
A thief.

00:41:44.168 --> 00:41:44.469
No.

00:41:45.568 --> 00:41:47.168
A great thief.

00:41:54.568 --> 00:41:55.969
Oh, he's awake.

00:41:56.769 --> 00:41:57.868
Back with us, eh?

00:41:59.068 --> 00:42:00.667
We didn't even have to touch you.

00:42:00.668 --> 00:42:03.668
???
and knocked yourself out.

00:42:04.168 --> 00:42:06.769
It was like watching Jerry Lewis
trying to stack chairs.

00:42:07.068 --> 00:42:08.269
Who are you?

00:42:08.469 --> 00:42:08.969
What do you want...

00:42:12.868 --> 00:42:15.568
I used to think your friend Gordon 
sent me...

00:42:16.269 --> 00:42:17.068
Gordon?

00:42:17.068 --> 00:42:17.967
Oh, come on.

00:42:17.969 --> 00:42:20.168
...because he asked me to track you down

00:42:20.769 --> 00:42:22.568
and put a bullet in your brain.

00:42:23.368 --> 00:42:24.868
Great. That sounds like him.

00:42:25.168 --> 00:42:26.568
But

00:42:26.668 --> 00:42:28.469
as it turns out...

00:42:30.368 --> 00:42:32.668
I'm on a mission from God.

00:42:33.368 --> 00:42:34.269
Look, Bela.

00:42:34.368 --> 00:42:36.568
My brother, he... touched the foot.

00:42:37.269 --> 00:42:39.568
And when you took it from him,
his luck went from...

00:42:39.568 --> 00:42:41.168
I know how it works.

00:42:41.368 --> 00:42:43.769
So, then you know he's gonna die
unless we can destroy it.

00:42:43.969 --> 00:42:44.969
Oh.

00:42:47.168 --> 00:42:48.368
You can have the foot...

00:42:49.469 --> 00:42:50.868
For $1.5 million.

00:42:51.969 --> 00:42:52.769
Nice.

00:42:52.969 --> 00:42:54.668
Yeah. I'll just call my banker.

00:42:56.469 --> 00:42:58.068
How'd you even find the damn thing,

00:42:58.469 --> 00:43:00.167
stuck in the back of some storage place,

00:43:00.168 --> 00:43:01.168
middle of nowhere?

00:43:05.969 --> 00:43:08.969
I just asked a few of the ghosts
of the people it had killed.

00:43:09.368 --> 00:43:11.668
They were very tuned in to its location.

00:43:12.668 --> 00:43:14.367
So you're only after yourself, huh?

00:43:14.368 --> 00:43:15.668
It's all about number one.

00:43:15.969 --> 00:43:18.269
Being a hunter is so much more noble?

00:43:19.469 --> 00:43:21.867
A bunch of obsessed, 
revenge-driven sociopaths

00:43:21.868 --> 00:43:23.868
trying to save a world 
that can't be saved.

00:43:24.269 --> 00:43:26.568
Well, aren't you
a glass half full.

00:43:27.168 --> 00:43:28.769
We're all going to hell, Dean.

00:43:29.469 --> 00:43:31.068
Might as well enjoy the ride.

00:43:31.068 --> 00:43:32.668
I actually agree with you there.

00:43:34.269 --> 00:43:38.168
Anyhoo, this has been charming,
but, uh, look at the time.

00:43:38.469 --> 00:43:39.368
Oh, and...

00:43:39.668 --> 00:43:40.368
This.

00:43:42.668 --> 00:43:44.867
You're not the only one
with sticky fingers.

00:43:44.868 --> 00:43:48.269
If it's any consolation, I think
you're a truly awful person.

00:44:15.168 --> 00:44:17.967
You were a part of that demon plan
to open the gate, weren't you?

00:44:17.969 --> 00:44:19.268
We did everything we could to stop it.

00:44:19.269 --> 00:44:20.769
Lie, lie, lie!

00:44:21.668 --> 00:44:22.868
You were in on it.

00:44:23.068 --> 00:44:24.967
You know what they're next move
is, too, don't you?

00:44:24.969 --> 00:44:27.769
No, I don't, okay?
You're wrong about all of this.

00:44:27.969 --> 00:44:29.568
Where are they gonna hit us next?

00:44:32.469 --> 00:44:33.568
Where?!

00:44:38.269 --> 00:44:40.568
Gordon told me about you, Sam,

00:44:40.769 --> 00:44:42.368
about your powers.

00:44:43.168 --> 00:44:46.167
You're some kind of
weirdo psychic freak.

00:44:46.168 --> 00:44:47.167
No, not anymore.

00:44:47.168 --> 00:44:49.167
I have no powers, no visions... nothing.

00:44:49.168 --> 00:44:50.668
- It just...
- Lie!

00:44:52.368 --> 00:44:55.668
Now no more lies.

00:44:55.969 --> 00:44:57.867
There's an army of demons out there,

00:44:57.868 --> 00:45:00.168
pushing at a world already on the brink.

00:45:01.668 --> 00:45:03.769
we're on deck 
for the end game here, right?

00:45:04.269 --> 00:45:05.368
So maybe,

00:45:06.068 --> 00:45:07.769
just maybe you can understand

00:45:09.568 --> 00:45:11.068
why we can't take chances.

00:45:11.068 --> 00:45:12.167
Whoa! Okay, okay.

00:45:12.168 --> 00:45:13.768
- Now, hold on a minute.
- Kubrick, get...

00:45:13.769 --> 00:45:15.969
No! You saw what happened, Creedie.

00:45:16.168 --> 00:45:17.368
Ask yourself...

00:45:17.868 --> 00:45:19.269
Why are we here?

00:45:19.769 --> 00:45:21.868
Because you saw a picture on the web?

00:45:22.068 --> 00:45:25.068
Because we chose this motel
instead of another?

00:45:25.868 --> 00:45:27.768
Luck like that doesn't just happen.

00:45:27.769 --> 00:45:28.967
Look, I can explain all of that.

00:45:28.969 --> 00:45:30.168
Shut up.

00:45:31.769 --> 00:45:33.068
It's God, Creedie.

00:45:33.269 --> 00:45:35.068
He led us here for one reason...

00:45:35.568 --> 00:45:36.868
To do his work.

00:45:37.969 --> 00:45:40.469
This is destiny.

00:45:40.769 --> 00:45:41.368
Whoa.

00:45:41.868 --> 00:45:42.568
No.

00:45:43.269 --> 00:45:44.269
No destiny.

00:45:45.469 --> 00:45:46.668
Just a rabbit's foot.

00:45:48.568 --> 00:45:49.867
Put the gun down, son,

00:45:49.868 --> 00:45:52.068
or you're gonna be
scraping brain off the wall.

00:45:52.668 --> 00:45:53.469
Oh, this thing?

00:45:54.769 --> 00:45:55.769
Yeah, that thing.

00:45:57.168 --> 00:45:57.969
Okay.

00:45:58.769 --> 00:46:01.069
But, you see, there's something
about me that you don't know.

00:46:03.168 --> 00:46:04.469
Yeah? What would that be?

00:46:05.769 --> 00:46:06.969
It's my lucky day.

00:46:09.469 --> 00:46:11.969
Oh, my God!
Did you see that shot?!

00:46:16.769 --> 00:46:17.668
I'm amazing.

00:46:23.668 --> 00:46:24.668
I'm Batman.

00:46:27.368 --> 00:46:28.368
Yeah.

00:46:28.668 --> 00:46:29.569
You're Batman.

00:46:35.668 --> 00:46:36.469
All right.

00:46:37.668 --> 00:46:38.969
Bone ash,

00:46:39.269 --> 00:46:40.569
cayenne pepper.

00:46:40.868 --> 00:46:41.769
That should do it.

00:46:41.868 --> 00:46:42.868
One second.

00:46:43.168 --> 00:46:43.667
Dean...

00:46:43.668 --> 00:46:45.168
Hey, back off, jinx.

00:46:45.668 --> 00:46:46.868
I'm bringing home the bacon.

00:46:51.868 --> 00:46:52.868
All right.

00:46:54.368 --> 00:46:57.668
Say goodbye to "Wascawy Wabbit."

00:47:00.269 --> 00:47:02.168
I think you'll find that belongs to me.

00:47:04.168 --> 00:47:04.969
Or, you know...

00:47:05.868 --> 00:47:06.769
Whatever.

00:47:10.168 --> 00:47:11.668
Put the foot down, honey.

00:47:12.569 --> 00:47:13.469
No.

00:47:14.668 --> 00:47:16.469
You're not gonna shoot anybody.

00:47:17.769 --> 00:47:20.168
See, I happen to be able to read people.

00:47:21.168 --> 00:47:23.168
Okay, you're a thief. fine.
But you're not...

00:47:23.569 --> 00:47:24.368
Oh!

00:47:26.069 --> 00:47:26.768
Son of a...

00:47:26.769 --> 00:47:28.668
Back off, tiger.

00:47:29.469 --> 00:47:30.569
Back off.

00:47:30.769 --> 00:47:32.969
You make one more move,
and I'll pull the trigger.

00:47:35.168 --> 00:47:37.569
You've got the luck, Dean.
You I can't hit.

00:47:38.569 --> 00:47:39.569
But your brother...

00:47:40.168 --> 00:47:41.569
Him I can't miss.

00:47:43.969 --> 00:47:45.569
What the hell is wrong with you?!

00:47:45.868 --> 00:47:47.868
You don't just do around
shooting people like that!

00:47:47.868 --> 00:47:48.868
Relax.

00:47:48.969 --> 00:47:50.868
It's a shoulder hit. I can aim.

00:47:51.769 --> 00:47:52.969
Besides,

00:47:53.269 --> 00:47:55.269
who here hasn't shot a few people?

00:47:57.969 --> 00:48:00.768
Put the rabbit's foot on the ground now.

00:48:00.769 --> 00:48:01.668
All right!

00:48:01.868 --> 00:48:02.769
All right.

00:48:03.269 --> 00:48:04.269
Take it easy.

00:48:10.569 --> 00:48:11.269
Think fast.

00:48:15.069 --> 00:48:16.269
Damn.

00:48:18.469 --> 00:48:19.368
Now,

00:48:20.168 --> 00:48:22.868
what do you say we destroy
that ugly-ass piece of dead thing?

00:48:27.569 --> 00:48:28.868
Thanks very much.

00:48:33.569 --> 00:48:35.068
I'm out $1.5 million

00:48:35.069 --> 00:48:38.469
and on the bad side of a very powerful,
fairly psychotic buyer.

00:48:38.569 --> 00:48:39.569
Wow.

00:48:39.769 --> 00:48:41.667
I really don't feel bad about that.

00:48:41.668 --> 00:48:42.569
Sam?

00:48:42.668 --> 00:48:43.469
No.

00:48:43.969 --> 00:48:45.269
Not even a little.

00:48:49.569 --> 00:48:50.868
Maybe next time,

00:48:51.469 --> 00:48:53.168
I'll hang you out to dry.

00:48:53.769 --> 00:48:56.269
Oh, don't go away angry. Just go away.

00:48:57.769 --> 00:48:59.269
Have a nice night, boys.

00:49:12.769 --> 00:49:13.569
You good?

00:49:14.168 --> 00:49:15.168
I'll live.

00:49:15.668 --> 00:49:17.569
I guess we're back to normal now, huh?

00:49:18.269 --> 00:49:19.368
No good luck.

00:49:19.368 --> 00:49:20.668
No bad luck.

00:49:21.569 --> 00:49:22.469
Oh,

00:49:23.469 --> 00:49:25.967
I forgot. We're at $46,000.

00:49:25.969 --> 00:49:27.969
I almost forgot about the...

00:49:28.969 --> 00:49:30.269
scratch tickets.

00:49:50.569 --> 00:49:52.168
Son of a bitch!

00:49:56.368 --> 00:49:58.168
You were right about everything.

00:49:59.168 --> 00:50:01.668
Sam Winchester is more than a monster.

00:50:02.469 --> 00:50:04.269
He's the adversary.

00:50:04.769 --> 00:50:06.469
And what was it that convinced you?

00:50:06.769 --> 00:50:08.368
God led me to him...

00:50:09.569 --> 00:50:11.569
And his will is clear.

00:50:13.969 --> 00:50:16.069
Okay.

00:50:17.769 --> 00:50:18.668
That's great.

00:50:19.368 --> 00:50:20.969
I'm glad to have you on board.

00:50:21.368 --> 00:50:23.368
But, uh, first things first.

00:50:25.469 --> 00:50:27.368
We got to get me the hell out of here.

00:50:28.069 --> 00:50:29.969
'cause like i told you before,

00:50:30.668 --> 00:50:32.967
Sam Winchester must die.

